{{multiple image |align=right |total_width=270 |image1=David Guetta 2012.jpg |image2=Bebe Rexha - Untold 2023 - 53113724212 (cropped).jpg |footer="I'm Good (Blue)" marks the fourth collaboration between [[David Guetta]] and [[Bebe Rexha]].<ref name="FCBDB"/>}}

In 2017, David Guetta and Bebe Rexha began working on "I'm Good (Blue)" without intending to release it at the time.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Brandle |first=Lars |magazine=Billboard |title=David Guetta and Bebe Rexha Are 'Good' at No. 1 In Australia |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-good-no-1-australia-aria-1235140103/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018161646/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-good-no-1-australia-aria-1235140103/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=16 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Aniftos |first=Rania |magazine=Billboard |title=Bebe Rexha Talks 'I'm Good (Blue),' Beyoncé, Grammy Nomination & More |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-grammy-nominations-1235212087/ |access-date=14 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230207191502/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-grammy-nominations-1235212087/ |archive-date=7 February 2023 |date=4 February 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2022, a snippet of the song garnered sudden popularity on the social media platform [[TikTok]], prompting Guetta and Rexha to eventually finalise the song.<ref name="Mier">{{cite magazine |last=Mier |first=Tomás |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |title=TikTok Helps Bebe Rexha and David Guetta Bring Back a Throwaway Remix of Club Classic 'Blue' |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/bebe-rexha-and-david-guetta-drop-feel-good-blue-1234581770/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018163158/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/bebe-rexha-and-david-guetta-drop-feel-good-blue-1234581770/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Rys |first=Dan |magazine=Billboard |title='Good' As Gold: How David Guetta and Bebe Rexha's TikTok Smash Became a Global Hit |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-warner-eric-wong-executive-of-week/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018161818/https://www.billboard.com/pro/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-warner-eric-wong-executive-of-week/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=16 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> Rexha described the start of the collaborative effort as a "last-second session the day of".<ref name="Mahjouri">{{cite web |last=Mahjouri |first=Shakiel |website=Edm.com |title=How Bebe Rexha and David Guetta's Complex Bond Creates 'Incredible Chemistry' |url=https://edm.com/features/bebe-rexha-interview-david-guetta-las-vegas-jbl-fest |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018163019/https://edm.com/features/bebe-rexha-interview-david-guetta-las-vegas-jbl-fest |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=13 October 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> As she explained, it all started with an unplanned message on social media, while Guetta was working on a recording and writing session in London.<ref name="Mahjouri"/> Guetta then played Rexha a remix of a song by Italian group [[Eiffel 65]], and they started having fun with it, without any expectation of it turning into a finished song.<ref name="Mahjouri"/> Leading up to its premiere, they published several videos on their respective TikTok accounts in August 2022, with Rexha [[Lip sync|lip-syncing]] along to the song and Guetta playing it at the [[Ultra Music Festival]] in 2017, with a caption that read, "Should we release it?".<ref name="Mier"/><ref>{{cite web |last=Medina |first=Dani |publisher=[[IHeartMedia|iHeart]] |title=Song Bebe Rexha & David Guetta Made Years Ago Is Finally Being Released |url=https://www.iheart.com/content/2022-08-20-bebe-rexha-david-guetta-viral-tiktok-song-blue-remix-im-good-release-date/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018195257/https://www.iheart.com/content/2022-08-20-bebe-rexha-david-guetta-viral-tiktok-song-blue-remix-im-good-release-date/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=20 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> The song marks the fourth collaboration between Guetta and Rexha, after "[[Hey Mama (David Guetta song)|Hey Mama]]" (2015), "[[Say My Name (David Guetta, Bebe Rexha and J Balvin song)|Say My Name]]" (2018) and "Family" (2021), most of whom achieved commercial success.<ref name="FCBDB">{{cite web |publisher=[[Warner Music Group|Warner]] |title=David Guetta & Bebe Rexha veröffentlichen ihren Viralhit "I'm Good (Blue)" |url=https://www.warnermusic.de/news/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-veroeffentlichen-ihren-viralhit-i-m-good-blue |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220829112905/https://www.warnermusic.de/news/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-veroeffentlichen-ihren-viralhit-i-m-good-blue |archive-date=29 August 2022 |language=de |date=29 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> What A DJ and [[Warner Records|Warner]] released "I'm Good (Blue)" for [[Music download|digital download]] and [[Streaming media|streaming]] in various countries on 26 August.<ref name="Release">Citations regarding the release of "I'm Good (Blue)" by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha in various selected countries:
*{{cite web |publisher=[[Apple Music]] (Australia) |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://music.apple.com/au/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018153443/https://music.apple.com/au/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}
*{{cite web |publisher=Apple Music (Canada) |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://music.apple.com/ca/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018153640/https://music.apple.com/ca/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}
*{{cite web |publisher=Apple Music (New Zealand) |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://music.apple.com/nz/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018153607/https://music.apple.com/nz/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}
*{{cite web |publisher=Apple Music (United Kingdom) |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://music.apple.com/gb/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018153727/https://music.apple.com/gb/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}
*{{cite web |publisher=Apple Music (United States) |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://music.apple.com/us/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018151025/https://music.apple.com/us/album/im-good-blue-single/1640751219 |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> The single, accompanied by remixes from notable artists such as French disc jockey [[Cedric Gervais]], Italian [[Gabry Ponte]] and Dutch [[Tiësto]], was published between from September to October 2022.<ref name="Remix 1"/><ref name="Remix 2"/> An acoustic rendition of the song, incorporating guitars and vocals, followed in January 2023.<ref name="Pepe"/><ref name="Acoustic"/><ref>{{cite web |last=Stone |first=Megan |publisher=[[WAPE-FM|Wape]] |title=New Music Friday: David Guetta, Bebe Rexha, Fletcher and Owl City |url=https://www.wape.com/news/new-music-friday/XNZSBIR4ENCSIGJPGEJJYAFKHA/ |access-date=6 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230106214944/https://www.wape.com/news/new-music-friday/XNZSBIR4ENCSIGJPGEJJYAFKHA/ |archive-date=6 January 2023 |date=6 January 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> Furthermore, the song was included on Rexha's third studio album, ''[[Bebe (album)|Bebe]]'' (2023).<ref>{{cite web |last=Garcia |first=Thania |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |title=Bebe Rexha Is Throwing a '70s Eurodance Party With Guests Dolly Parton, Snoop Dogg |url=https://variety.com/2023/music/news/bebe-rexha-new-album-dolly-parton-1235593506/ |access-date=21 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121200756/https://variety.com/2023/music/news/bebe-rexha-new-album-dolly-parton-1235593506/ |archive-date=21 November 2023 |date=28 April 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>

"I'm Good (Blue)" was written by Guetta, Rexha, [[Jeffrey Jey|Gianfranco Randone]], [[Kamille (musician)|Kamille]], Massimo Gabutti, [[Maurizio Lobina]] and [[Phil Plested|Plested]], and was produced by Guetta and [[Timofey Reznikov]].<ref name="Spotify">{{cite web |publisher=[[Spotify]] |title=I'm Good (Blue){{spaced ndash}}Single by David Guetta and Bebe Rexha |url=https://open.spotify.com/track/4uUG5RXrOk84mYEfFvj3cK |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018200407/https://open.spotify.com/track/4uUG5RXrOk84mYEfFvj3cK |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 August 2022 |url-status=live}} ''Note: Click on the three dots on the right of the track to display the credits.''</ref> It is composed in the key of [[G minor]] and [[time signature]] of common time with a [[tempo]] of 128 [[beats per minute]].<ref name="Musicnotes">{{cite web |publisher=Musicnotes.com |title=David Guetta and Bebe Rexha 'I'm Good (Blue)' Sheet Music |date=23 November 2022 |url=https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0266373 |access-date=16 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221216223153/https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0266373 |archive-date=16 December 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> The song follows in the [[chord progression]] of Gm in the intro, Gm–F/G–EG-Cm/G-Gm-F/G-EG in the chorus and E♭-Cm-Gm-F-E♭ in the verse.<ref name="Musicnotes"/> It is an [[Beat (music)|upbeat]] [[dance-pop]],<ref name="Songtexte">{{cite web |website=Songtexte.com |title=Wovon handelt 'I'm Good (Blue)' von David Guetta und Bebe Rexha? |url=https://www.songtexte.com/news/wovon-handelt-im-good-blue-von-david-guetta-und-bebe-rexha |access-date=19 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221019175722/https://www.songtexte.com/news/wovon-handelt-im-good-blue-von-david-guetta-und-bebe-rexha |archive-date=19 October 2022 |language=de |date=19 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Papadatos">{{cite web |last=Papadatos |first=Markos |work=Digital Journal |title=Review: David Guetta and Bebe Rexha release dazzling music video for 'I'm Good (Blue)' |url=https://www.digitaljournal.com/entertainment/review-david-guetta-and-bebe-rexha-release-stunning-music-video-for-im-good-blue/article |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018162045/https://www.digitaljournal.com/entertainment/review-david-guetta-and-bebe-rexha-release-stunning-music-video-for-im-good-blue/article |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=25 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> which [[Interpolation (popular music)|interpolates]] Italian group [[Eiffel 65]]'s single "[[Blue (Da Ba Dee)]]" (1998).<ref>{{cite web |publisher=Musikfreitag |title=David Guetta, Bebe Rexha{{spaced ndash}}'I'm Good (Blue)' |url=https://musikfreitag.com/2022/08/28/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018164348/https://musikfreitag.com/2022/08/28/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |language=de |date=28 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Brandle |first=Lars |magazine=Billboard |title=David Guetta and Bebe Rexha's 'I'm Good (Blue)' Climbs to U.K. Chart Summit |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-uk-singles-chart-1235144502/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018161303/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-uk-singles-chart-1235144502/ |archive-date=18 October 2022 |date=26 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Aniftos |first=Rania |magazine=Billboard |title=Here Are the Lyrics to David Guetta & Bebe Rexha's 'I'm Good (Blue)' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/lyrics/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-lyrics-1235152898/ |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221013160727/https://www.billboard.com/music/lyrics/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-blue-lyrics-1235152898/ |archive-date=13 October 2022 |date=10 July 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>   The vocal range of Rexha in the song spans from a low note of [[D (musical note)|D<sub>3</sub>]] to a high note of [[F (musical note)|F<sub>5</sub>]].<ref name="Musicnotes"/> The lyrics of the song captures Rexha's anticipation of a long clubbing night ahead.<ref name="Songtexte"/> She showcases her good mood and excitement of having one of the best nights, singing lines such as, "I'm good, yeah, I'm feelin' alright/ Baby, I'ma have the best freaking night of my life/ And wherever it takes me, I'm down for the ride."<ref name="Songtexte"/><ref name="Vielrose">{{cite web |last=Vielrose |first=Veronika |publisher=[[Westdeutscher Rundfunk]] (WDR) |title=David Guetta & Bebe Rexha{{spaced ndash}}'I'm Good (Blue)' |url=https://www1.wdr.de/radio/1live/musik/neu-fuer-den-sektor/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-100.html |access-date=18 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221018163927/https://www1.wdr.de/radio/1live/musik/neu-fuer-den-sektor/david-guetta-bebe-rexha-im-good-100.html |archive-date=18 October 2022 |language=de |date=9 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>

